---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="Reviewer store" description="A controlled environment for testing the HonorCart browser extension."><PageHero eyebrow="Extension review environment" title="Test HonorCart without a real purchase." lead="This controlled page lets browser-extension reviewers verify coupon lookup, referral stand-down behavior, and disabled monetization. No products are sold and no coupon is redeemable."/><section class="section shell"><div class="three-grid"><article class="plain-card"><h2>1. Enable HonorCart</h2><p>Install the beta extension, review its privacy disclosure, and enable coupon lookup.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h2>2. Find the test coupon</h2><p>Open HonorCart on this page and choose <strong>Find coupons</strong>. It returns the deterministic reviewer code <code>HONOR10</code>.</p></article><article class="plain-card"><h2>3. Verify stand-down</h2><p>Open the protected-session link below in a new tab. HonorCart should display <strong>Existing referral protected</strong> and keep activation disabled.</p></article></div></section><section class="section soft"><div class="shell two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">Unclaimed session</p><h2>No referral marker</h2><p>The extension should recognize this reviewer store, return the test coupon, and report that no existing referral was detected. Monetization remains disabled.</p><a class="button" href="/reviewer-store">Open clean test session</a></div><div><p class="eyebrow">Protected session</p><h2>Supported referral marker</h2><p>The <code>afsrc=1</code> marker represents an existing affiliate referral. HonorCart must stand down for this tab.</p><a class="button" href="/reviewer-store?afsrc=1">Open protected test session</a></div></div></section><section class="callout shell"><h2>Safety state</h2><p>The global monetization switch and this test merchant’s monetization approval are both off. The activation API returns <code>403 monetization_disabled</code>, even after deliberate user action.</p><a href="/transparency">Read the public stand-down policy →</a></section></SiteLayout>
